1
00:04:25,263 --> 00:04:31,263
A high-voltage thriller!

2
00:08:50,526 --> 00:08:56,526
Demolition High is a action film directed by Jim Wynorski.

3
00:13:15,789 --> 00:13:21,789
When a group of terrorists (led by Luther) take over a high school making the students in it their hostages, it is up to several of the students
(led by Lenny) to help prevent disaster while the authorities (Slater and General Wainwright) do their part on the other side.

4
00:17:41,052 --> 00:17:47,052
Lenny Slater, played by Corey Haim.

5
00:22:06,315 --> 00:22:12,315
Slater, played by Alan Thicke.

6
00:26:31,578 --> 00:26:37,578
General Wainwright, played by Dick Van Patten.

7
00:30:56,842 --> 00:31:02,842
Luther, played by Jeff Kober.

8
00:35:22,105 --> 00:35:28,105
Tanya, played by Melissa Brasselle.

9
00:39:47,368 --> 00:39:53,368
Stacy, played by Kimberley Roberts.

10
00:44:12,631 --> 00:44:18,631
Demolition Man is a 1993 American science fiction action film
directed by Marco Brambilla in his directorial debut.

11
00:48:37,894 --> 00:48:43,894
It stars Sylvester Stallone, Wesley Snipes, Sandra Bullock, and Nigel Hawthorne.

12
00:53:03,157 --> 00:53:09,157
Stallone plays John Spartan, a risk-taking police officer with a
reputation for causing destruction while carrying out his work.

13
00:57:28,421 --> 00:57:34,421
After a failed attempt to rescue hostages from evil crime lord Simon Phoenix
(Snipes), they are both sentenced to be cryogenically frozen in 1996.

14
01:01:53,684 --> 01:01:59,684
In 2032, Phoenix escapes and the authorities awaken Spartan to help capture him.

15
01:06:18,947 --> 01:06:24,947
The story makes allusions to many other works, including Aldous
Huxley's 1932 dystopian novel Brave New World and H.

16
01:10:44,210 --> 01:10:50,210
Wells's The Sleeper Awakes.

17
01:15:09,473 --> 01:15:15,473
The film was released in the United States on October
8, 1993, to mixed reviews from critics.

18
01:19:34,736 --> 01:19:40,736
It earned $159 million worldwide, and was
considered a successful film for Stallone.
